{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504521-blue-bloods-pure-sovereigns-2e-conversion","id":1504521,"title":"Blue Bloods (Pure Sovereigns 2e conversion)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-05T18:35:10-08:00","id":1504521,"title":"Blue Bloods (Pure Sovereigns 2e conversion)","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><u><b>Pure Sovereigns</b></u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Blue Bloods</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Pages 168-170 of Silver Ladder for lore<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Path:</b> Obrimos<br /> <b>Parent Order: </b>Silver Ladder<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Life 2, Mind 1, 2 dots in Expression, Status 3 or Mystery Cult Initiation 3, one of the following additional skills at 2 dots or higher: Athletics, Persuasion, Politics, Socialize<br /> <b>Initiation: </b>Rigorously work on your body and mind for a week while meditating on the goal of becoming a suitable ruler according to the legacies philosophy.<br /> <b>Ruling Arcana:</b> Life<br /> <b>Yantras:</b> Classical monarchal symbols (+1); Giving a command and having it followed (+1, +2 if a roll is needed); Attend of social or political function where you are seen as the rightful leader of the space (+2)<br /> <b>Oblations:</b> Practicing yoga or martial arts; spend an hour meditating on part of a long term goal; asserting your ability to lead a group.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Attainments</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>First Attainment: Eye's of Stars</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Prerequisites: Initiation</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">By attuning themselves to the present moment Blue Bloods have an increased awareness of their surroundings. After meditating for an hour or while acting as a group leader that they have at least three dots of status in this attainment is activated, acting like \u201cHeightened Senses\u201d (Life 1, MtAw 148) with reach for advanced duration.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Optional: Mind 1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Pure Sovereigns shape their souls to rule and part of this rule is recognizing other kings. By studying someone for a turn they are able to glean information about the rule of others. This attainment allows the Blue Blood to learn the highest level status per potency of the attainment, from highest to lowest.<br /> <br /> <b>Second Attainment: Blood of Silver</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Prerequisites: Life 2, 3 dots in Expression</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">This early on in their journey the Pure Sovereigns gain complete control over their bodily functions. After meditating for an hour or while acting as a group leader that they have at least three dots of status in, this attainment is activated, acting like \u201cBody Control\u201d (Life 2, MtAw 148) with reach for advanced duration.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Optional: Mind 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">In order to do their work and trust in themselves Blue Bloods learn to forget their own failures. This can lead some to become arrogant and believe themselves infallible. This attainment takes an hour of meditation to activate and functions like \u201cMemory Hole (Mind 2, MtAw 160) with reach for advanced duration. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Third Attainment: Flesh of Gold</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Prerequisites: Life 3, The optional skill used to meet the requirements of initiation must be raised to 3 or a second option from the list must be raised to 2<br /> This attainment makes the Pure Sovereign\u2019s body worthy of the queen that she is. By spending an hour of meditation or by acting as a group leader that they have at least three dots of status in, this attainment activates, acting as \u201cHoning the Form\u201d (Life 3, MtAw 150) with reach for advanced duration.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Optional: Mind 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">In addition to the above effect, the Blue Blood\u2019s mind also advances to match her status as queen, functioning like \u201cAugment Mind\u201d (Mind 3, MtAw 161) with reach for advanced duration.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fourth Attainment: Mind of Thunder</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Prerequisites: Life 4, 4 dots in expression</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Everyone has a different idea of what a queen looks like, old and wise, powerful and worldly, humble and kind. This attainment lets the Blue Blood take on whatever form they wish to meet that image. At will or while acting as a group leader they have at least three dots of status in the attainment activities, functioning like \u201cMany Faces\u201d (Life 4, MtAw 150) with reach for instant casting and advanced duration.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Optional: Mind 4</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Queens do not need to sleep, at least not those who rule well. This attainment allows the mage to gain all the benefits of sleep, feeling rested, memories, and gaining willpower, without the need to sleep. Should the mage wish to sleep for any reason they remember their dreams and can awaken whenever they wish.<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth Attainment: Incarnation of Diamond</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Prerequisites:</span>\u200b <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Life 5, The optional skill used to meet the requirements of initiation must be raised to 4 or a second option from the list must be raised to 3 or a third option must be raised to 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Blue blood can heal any damage they take so that they may always be fit to serve. This attainment instantly heals bashing damage equal to potency x2, lethal damage equal to potency, and any physical tilts they may suffer.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Optional: Mind 5</span>\u200b<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The mental toil of ruling can be great, so the final step of the attainment is learning to let go of failure. This attainment allows the mage to permanently remove one mental tilt or condition after an hour of meditation, or while serving as a group leader that they have at least three dots of status in.</span><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 11-16-2024, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T18:37:54-08:00","id":1504522,"title":"","content":"So I tried with these guys two because they will be important in my chronicle with a few high profile NPCs being among them.<br /> <br /> I tried to stay clear of letting their mind magic influence others to the best of my ability, wanting it to be about the mage becoming better internally. There is some obvious gray area there but I'm happy with it. The reason for this is because a different legacy, the &quot;right of kings&quot; one from N&amp;A, I want to finish building as well and I want to make their mind attainments about the influence of others as a stark contrast in the philosophy of what it means to be a monarch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T19:44:54-08:00","id":1504525,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:8px\">(Shameless self-promotion - I did a <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e?p=1484955#post1484955\">Sovereigns update</a> a while back)</span><br /> <br /> I think you might be leaning a bit harder into the &quot;rulership&quot; aspect of the Blue Bloods than the original intended. The writeup in Silver Ladder makes an effort to emphasize that the majority of them are goal-oriented, and took to the Legacy for the pysical and psychological benefits of longevity and enhanced congition. Would-be rulers are a camp within them, certainly, but self-mastery is the driving force. That makes the Status requirement -and focus withing the Attainments- you've given them kinda at odds with it. They're meant to be great leaders as a side-consequence of self-refinement, rather than becoming refined through great leadership.<br /> <br /> Granted, you've stated you want them to be a counterpoint to the Tyrion Archons, and in that I understand leaning into the &quot;Sovereigns&quot; portion of their name. The Attainments you've created are generally good - I'm curious about the Mind 2 Attainment though. It appears to function like a combination of <u>First Impressions</u> and <u>Incognito Presence</u>, in that it's basically <u>First Impressions</u> that affects everyone who perceives the user. Both of those spells are Duration-primary, meaning that at best it will have a Potency of 3. The average person will have a Composure of 2, so it will only have a net boost of one step. Not something to sniff at, certainly, but not exactly impressive. I'm assuming it functions on an Advanced Duration? In which case it's lasting for a day when first learned and a year at maximum - you'll rarely need to refresh it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T19:53:11-08:00","id":1504526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504521-blue-bloods-pure-sovereigns-2e-conversion?p=1504525#post1504525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">(Shameless self-promotion - I did a <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e?p=1484955#post1484955\">Sovereigns update</a> a while back)</span><br /> <br /> Granted, you've stated you want them to be a counterpoint to the Tyrion Archons, and in that I understand leaning into the &quot;Sovereigns&quot; portion of their name. The Attainments you've created are generally good - I'm curious about the Mind 2 Attainment though. It appears to function like a combination of <u>First Impressions</u> and <u>Incognito Presence</u>, in that it's basically <u>First Impressions</u> that affects everyone who perceives the user. Both of those spells are Duration-primary, meaning that at best it will have a Potency of 3. The average person will have a Composure of 2, so it will only have a net boost of one step. Not something to sniff at, certainly, but not exactly impressive. I'm assuming it functions on an Advanced Duration? In which case it's lasting for a day when first learned and a year at maximum - you'll rarely need to refresh it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Make your self promotion larger pls I missed it until I quoted this and it isn't a competition, let people see yours.<br /> <br /> I'm glad that's the attainment you took issue with because its actually my least on here. It fits the theme but eh.....not really what I want. Probably going to change it at some point tomorrow.<br /> <br /> I think you might be leaning a bit harder into the &quot;rulership&quot; aspect of the Blue Bloods than the original intended. The writeup in Silver Ladder makes an effort to emphasize that the majority of them are goal-oriented, and took to the Legacy for the pysical and psychological benefits of longevity and enhanced congition. Would-be rulers are a camp within them, certainly, but self-mastery is the driving force. That makes the Status requirement -and focus withing the Attainments- you've given them kinda at odds with it. They're meant to be great leaders as a side-consequence of self-refinement, rather than becoming refined through great leadership.<br /> <br /> While I feel like the language isn't there, I do think, with the exception of the status feature I included, I think its still there in theme, their body and mind are refined, sharp, and ready for them to complete whatever goal they set themselves too. I leaned into the language because, well, I like it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 03-05-2023, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T19:54:16-08:00","id":1504527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504521-blue-bloods-pure-sovereigns-2e-conversion?p=1504525#post1504525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">(Shameless self-promotion - I did a <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e?p=1484955#post1484955\">Sovereigns update</a> a while back)</span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Your naming method is amazing for them, I love it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T20:04:28-08:00","id":1504528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504521-blue-bloods-pure-sovereigns-2e-conversion?p=1504527#post1504527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your naming method is amazing for them, I love it</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, thanks, but I only made the name &quot;Mind of Amber&quot;. The original Legacy has &quot;Incarnation of Diamond&quot; as the capstone, so I split that into &quot;Incarnation of Thunder&quot; and &quot;The Diamond Involate&quot;.<br /> <br /> There's nothing wrong with the First Impressions Attainment you've created, so don't be too quick to remove it. You just might need to tweek it a bit. It mostly just needs Potency-primary, so the easierst options are to either move it up a slot, or give it a stricter limitation like &quot;only works on non-supernatural humans&quot;. That would disqualify most other splats, as well as their subordinate half-splats like Fae-Touched, Ghouls, Proximi, Wollf-blooded, ect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T19:17:21-08:00","id":1504703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504521-blue-bloods-pure-sovereigns-2e-conversion?p=1504528#post1504528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's nothing wrong with the First Impressions Attainment you've created, so don't be too quick to remove it. You just might need to tweek it a bit. It mostly just needs Potency-primary, so the easierst options are to either move it up a slot, or give it a stricter limitation like &quot;only works on non-supernatural humans&quot;. That would disqualify most other splats, as well as their subordinate half-splats like Fae-Touched, Ghouls, Proximi, Wollf-blooded, ect.</div> </div> </div> </div>After thinking on it during the work day I think I'm going to steal the idea from the 1e version that lets them &quot;forget&quot; their failures, because its kinda cool","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}